            EnChapter(1, "The Karamazov Family", listOf(
                "Fyodor Pavlovich Karamazov was a strange and despicable man, a man who had made his fortune by begging from the rich and cheating the poor, and who had spent his life in drunkenness and debauchery.",
                "He had been married twice, and both of his wives had died, and he had left behind three sons whom he had neglected for most of their lives.",
                "The eldest, Dmitri, had been raised by servants, and had become a wild and passionate young man, a soldier, a gambler, and a man of enormous appetites.",
                "The second, Ivan, had been raised by a benefactor, and had become a brilliant student, a philosopher, and a man who questioned everything, including God himself.",
                "The youngest, Alyosha, had been raised in a monastery, and had become a novice, a young man of great faith and great compassion, a man who loved everyone he met.",
                "And there was a fourth son, an illegitimate son named Smerdyakov, who had been raised as a servant in the Karamazov household, and who was silent and strange and utterly without love.",
                "The family was a family of contradictions, a family in which every son was at war with the father, and in which every son was at war with himself.",
                "And in the midst of this family, there was a woman named Katerina Ivanovna, a woman of great pride and great beauty, who had been engaged to Dmitri and who loved him desperately.",
                "There was also a woman named Grushenka, a woman of great beauty and great cunning, who was loved by both Fyodor and Dmitri, and who enjoyed the power that her beauty gave her over both of them.",
                "The story began, as all stories of this family began, with a quarrel, and the quarrel was about money, and the money was the inheritance that Fyodor owed to Dmitri.",
                "Dmitri came to his father to demand the money, and Fyodor refused to give it, and the two of them shouted at each other, and the whole household heard, and the whole town heard.",
                "And in that quarrel, a threat was made, and the threat was the threat of murder, and the threat would come to be at the center of everything that followed.",
                "For Dmitri had told his father, in the heat of his anger, that he would kill him, and the words had been heard by many witnesses, and the words would come back to haunt him.",
                "And so the first chapter of the Karamazov story began, with a family divided against itself, and with a murder waiting to happen, and with the whole world watching.",
                "The town in which the Karamazovs lived was a small town, a town in which everyone knew everyone, and in which every scandal was discussed in every home, and in which every secret was, in the end, no secret at all.",
                "The monastery, which stood on the edge of the town, was a place of silence and prayer, a place where the elder Zosima lived, a man of great wisdom and great love, a man to whom Alyosha had attached himself with all the devotion of his young and faithful heart.",
                "The monastery was also a place of controversy, for the elder Zosima was a man of new ideas, a man who believed that the church should not be separated from the world, and there were those who hated him for it.",
                "Among those who hated the elder was Ivan, who did not believe in God, and who could not forgive a world in which innocent children suffered, and who had come to the monastery not to seek faith but to argue against it.",
                "Among those who loved the elder was Alyosha, who believed with a simple and total faith, and who saw in the elder a father far better than the father who had abandoned him.",
                "And so the family gathered in the monastery, the father and the sons, and the argument that followed would set in motion the events that would destroy them all.",
