                "Ivan, the second son, was a man of cold intellect, a man who could reason his way through any problem except the problem of his own heart, a man who was tormented by questions that he could not answer.",
                "Alyosha, the youngest, was a man of warmth, a man who listened to everyone and judged no one, a man who carried in his heart a faith that no argument could shake.",
                "Smerdyakov, the servant, was a man of silence, a man whose silence was more disturbing than any word, a man who watched everything and said nothing and remembered everything.",
