            EnChapter(2, "The Murder", listOf(
                "The night of the murder was a night of confusion and horror, a night in which no one knew what was happening and everyone was convinced that they knew.",
                "Fyodor Pavlovich was alone in his house, waiting for Grushenka, for she had promised to come to him that night and he was certain that she would.",
                "Dmitri was also waiting, but not in the house, for he was hiding in the shadows of the garden, watching his father's window, waiting for Grushenka to arrive.",
                "Smerdyakov was in his room, pretending to be ill, pretending to be asleep, waiting for the moment when he would act.",
                "And Alyosha was also awake, for he had been sent to fetch Grushenka, and he was wandering through the streets of the town, wondering what he should do.",
                "Sometime after midnight, Fyodor was murdered, and his head was bashed in with a brass pestle, and his money was stolen, and the killer fled into the night.",
                "Dmitri was the first to be suspected, for he had the motive, and he had the opportunity, and he had made the threat.",
                "He was arrested, and he was tried, and he was convicted, and he was sentenced to twenty years of hard labor in Siberia.",
                "But Dmitri was not the murderer, and the real murderer was Smerdyakov, who had planned the crime, who had manipulated Dmitri, and who had finally executed his plan with cold and calculated precision.",
                "Smerdyakov confessed to Ivan, who was his half-brother, and Ivan was horrified by the confession, and he was horrified by the realization that he had been complicit in the murder.",
                "For Ivan had said, in a conversation with Smerdyakov, that if there were no God, then everything was permitted, and Smerdyakov had taken him at his word.",
                "And so the murder was not just Dmitri's tragedy, not just Fyodor's death, but the tragedy of the entire family, the tragedy of a family that had been divided against itself from the beginning.",
