                "And the murder was not just a death, but a revelation, a revelation of the truth that lies at the heart of every family, and at the heart of every human being.",
                "The house in which the murder took place was an old house, a house of dark corridors and locked doors, a house in which every sound echoed and every shadow seemed to move.",
                "Fyodor Pavlovich had lived in that house for years, and he had filled it with his drunkenness and his cruelty, and he had made it a place of fear for everyone who entered it.",
                "The servants of the house had learned to move silently, to speak only when spoken to, to disappear when the master was in one of his rages, and they had learned to fear him more than they feared anyone else.",
                "Smerdyakov, in particular, had learned to fear him, and to hate him, and to plan, in the silence of his room, the revenge that he would one day take.",
                "For Smerdyakov was not merely a servant, he was a son, a son who had been denied his father, a son who had been denied his name, a son who had been denied everything that a son should have.",
                "And so he had planned the murder, not with passion, but with calculation, not with anger, but with coldness, and he had waited for the moment when everything would be in place.",
