                "And so he left the tavern, and he went out into the night, and he walked through the streets of the town, and he did not know where he was going or why.",
                "And the question that he had asked in his poem, the question of whether there was a God, and whether, if there was no God, everything was permitted, remained unanswered.",
                "And the question would remain unanswered, through all the events that followed, through the murder and the trial and the confession and the death.",
                "And Ivan, who had asked the question, would be destroyed by it, for he could not live with the question, and he could not live without the answer.",
                "And so the chapter of the Grand Inquisitor came to an end, and the question that it raised would echo through the rest of the story, and through the rest of Ivan's life."
            )),
            EnChapter(4, "The Trial", listOf(
                "The trial of Dmitri Karamazov was the trial of the century, or at least the trial of the season, and the whole town attended, and the whole town had an opinion.",
                "The evidence was overwhelming, for Dmitri had been at the scene, and he had the money, and he had threatened his father, and there was no other suspect.",
                "The prosecutor was brilliant, and he wove the evidence into a story of greed and passion and murder, and the jury was moved, and the crowd was moved, and the verdict was inevitable.",
                "The defense was also brilliant, and the defense argued that Dmitri was a man of honor, that he had not killed his father, that the evidence was circumstantial.",
                "But the defense was not enough, and Dmitri was found guilty, and he was sentenced to twenty years of hard labor in Siberia.",
                "And Dmitri, hearing the verdict, did not protest, and did not weep, and did not curse, for he had accepted the punishment, and the punishment was a kind of salvation.",
                "For Dmitri had always known that he was a man of passion, and he had always known that his passions would destroy him, and he had always known that he would have to suffer for them.",
                "And the suffering was not just the sentence, but the suffering of his whole life, the suffering of his soul, the suffering of a man who had been at war with himself from the beginning.",
                "And the suffering was not just his own, but the suffering of his family, the suffering of Alyosha, who had loved him, and the suffering of Ivan, who had lost his mind, and the suffering of Katerina, who had loved him, and the suffering of Grushenka, who had finally loved him too late.",
                "And the suffering was not just the trial, but the trial was a symbol, a symbol of the judgment that every human being faces, a judgment not from a court, but from the truth of his own heart.",
                "For every human being is on trial, and the trial is the trial of his soul, and the verdict is the verdict of his own conscience, and the punishment is the punishment of his own guilt.",
                "And Dmitri, in the end, accepted this trial, and accepted this verdict, and accepted this punishment, and in the accepting, he found a peace that he had never known.",
                "And so the fourth chapter of the Karamazov story ended, with the trial, and with the verdict, and with the peace that comes only to those who have accepted the truth about themselves.",
                "The courtroom was crowded on the day of the trial, for the whole town had come to see the spectacle, and the spectacle was everything that the town had hoped for.",
                "The ladies in their fine dresses, the gentlemen in their dark coats, the journalists with their notebooks, the peasants with their simple clothes, all of them were there, all of them were watching.",
                "And in the midst of them all, the prisoner sat, in his dark coat, with his eyes on the ground, and he did not look at anyone, and he did not speak to anyone.",
                "The prosecutor rose, and he began his speech, and his speech was a masterpiece of accusation, a speech that wove together every piece of evidence into a single damning story.",
                "He spoke of the money, the three thousand rubles that Dmitri had taken, the money that his father had been saving for Grushenka, the money that was found on Dmitri after the murder.",
