                "And the door had opened, and she had passed through it, and on the other side she had found not the life that she had dreamed of but the life that she had always known.",
                "For Charles was not a man of the world, he was a country doctor, a man of simple habits and simple pleasures, a man who loved his wife in a simple and unromantic way.",
                "And Emma, who had wanted passion, had found routine, and Emma, who had wanted drama, had found boredom, and Emma, who had wanted love, had found only affection.",
                "And so the disappointment had begun, and the disappointment had grown, and the disappointment had become the central fact of her life, the fact from which all her other actions would flow.",
                "And from the disappointment came the restlessness, and from the restlessness came the affairs, and from the affairs came the debts, and from the debts came the ruin.",
                "And the ruin was not merely the ruin of Emma, but the ruin of Charles, and of Berthe, and of everyone who had ever loved her, and the ruin was the ruin of a whole world.",
                "And so the first chapter of Madame Bovary ended, and the chapter was a beginning, the beginning of a descent, a descent that would lead, in the end, to the death of the heroine.",
                "For the descent was not a fall from grace, but a fall from illusion, and the illusion was the illusion of a life that could be lived according to the rules of romance novels.",
                "And the fall was the fall that every human being must make, the fall from the dreams of youth to the realities of age, the fall that is not a tragedy but a necessity, the fall that is the beginning of wisdom."
